{"id":"u-bf9e8bfd-bb43-42aa-b85b-30e444490936","src":"community","title":"GZCL + VO2 Training","author":"Ron","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/gDtq3c-gzcl-vo2-1","desc":"This program is designed for lifters who want to combine strength, hypertrophy, and conditioning with a clear emphasis on aesthetics and performance. The focus is on building round, powerful glutes, fuller hamstrings, and capped shoulders while developing the upper chest for a balanced physique.\n\nTraining is structured around proven barbell strength lifts (squat, bench, deadlift, and overhead press) with accessory work programmed for hypertrophy in the target muscle groups. Each week includes:\n\nLower body specialization: Hip thrusts, Bulgarian split squats, RDLs, and cable abductions target the glutes from multiple angles and ranges of motion. Hamstrings are developed with both hip hinge and knee-flexion variations.\n\nShoulder development: Overhead presses, lateral raises, and rear delt flys create balanced growth across all three heads of the deltoid.\n\nUpper chest emphasis: Incline pressing and cable flys drive clavicular pec development for fullness and shape.\n\nConditioning: One high-intensity interval training (HIIT) session and one Zone 2 steady-state cardio session per week build cardiovascular fitness and VO₂max. A weekly LISS recovery session maintains endurance and active recovery.\n\nBalanced accessory work: Calf raises, ab training, and posterior chain movements round out the program for strength, stability, and aesthetics.\n\nThis program balances strength progression, hypertrophy-focused accessories, and cardiovascular training to maximize both physique and performance. Volume is distributed intelligently to prioritize glutes, hamstrings, shoulders, and upper chest, while managing CNS recovery for long-term sustainability.\n\nWhether your goal is to grow your physique, improve your conditioning, or simply build a strong and balanced body, this program provides the framework to do it efficiently.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":3,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-03-15T03:21:15.313Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4","Day 5","Day 6","Day 7"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":3,"pct":85,"x":5}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"pct":70,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hip Thrust (Barbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Single Arm Rear Delt Cable Fly","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":4}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"VO2 Max Intervals","sets":[{"sec":240,"x":4}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":3,"pct":85,"x":5}]},{"n":"Sumo Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"pct":70,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"One Arm Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Hip Thrust (Barbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Cable Hip Abduction","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lying Leg Raise","sets":[{"r":25,"x":4}]},{"n":"Oblique Crunch","sets":[{"r":25,"x":4}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Cardio (Zone 2)","sets":[{"sec":3600}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":3,"pct":85,"x":5}]},{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"pct":70,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"max":1,"r":15,"x":4}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Sumo Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":3,"pct":85,"x":5}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"pc